meta {
  name: Comment
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.add_ticket_comment
  body: formUrlEncoded
  auth: inherit
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  ticket: 12hnuea73s
  text: Testing Ticket comment
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("comment is in the returned ticket", function () {
    const c = res.body.message.comments;
    expect(c[c.length - 1].mine).to.equal(true);
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Adds a comment to a ticket.

  **Endpoint:** `POST /api/method/implementor.client_api.add_ticket_comment`
  **Screen:** Ticket status → Comment

  > ⚠️ **Changes data** on the shared server. Use test records only.

  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned. A **Client User** can only comment on tickets they raised.

  **Body fields (form-encoded):**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `ticket` | string | yes | `12hnuea73s` |  |
  | `text` | string | yes | `Testing Ticket comment` | Trimmed. Saved as plain text (HTML-escaped). |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  **Response (trimmed):**

  The updated ticket, in the same shape as **Ticket status**. The new comment is last in `comments[]`, with `mine: true`.

  ```json
  {
    "message": {
      "name": "12hnuea73s",
      "status": "in_progress",
      "comments": [
        { "id": "f4e5d6c7b8", "text": "Testing Ticket comment", "by": "Aisha Khan", "mine": true, "at": "2026-10-31T10:02:11+03:00" }
      ],
      ...
    }
  }
  ```

  **Errors:**

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403 `no_client_linked`:** the signed-in user is not linked to any client company.
  - **403 `not_permitted`:** another client company's ticket, a ticket raised by someone else (Client User), or `customer` sent for a company the user is not linked to.
  - **404 `not_found`:** ticket not found (or `customer` sent and does not exist).
  - **417 `missing_parameter`:** `ticket` missing or empty.
  - **417 `comment_required`:** `text` is empty or only spaces.

  **Notes:**

  - If the ticket is `waiting_on_client`, commenting moves it back to `in_progress`. Other statuses don't change.
  - `comments[].text` may contain HTML entities (e.g. `&amp;`); decode them before showing.
}
